<h2 id=3D"stateless-web-tier">Stateless web tier</h2>
<p>Now it is time to consider scaling the web tier horizontally. For this, =
we need to move state (for instance user session data) out of the web tier.=
 A good practice is to store session data in the persistent storage such as=
 relational database or NoSQL. Each web server in the cluster can access st=
ate data from databases. This is called stateless web tier.</p>
<h3 id=3D"stateful-architecture">Stateful architecture</h3>
<p>A stateful server and stateless server has some key differences. A state=
ful server remembers client data (state) from one request to the next. A st=
ateless server keeps no state information.</p>
<p>Figure 12 shows an example of a stateful architecture.</p>
