<p>In Figure 14, we move the session data out of the web tier and store the=
m in the persistent data store. The shared data store could be a relational=
 database, Memcached/Redis, NoSQL, etc. The NoSQL data store is chosen as i=
t is easy to scale. Autoscaling means adding or removing web servers automa=
tically based on the traffic load. After the state data is removed out of w=
eb servers, auto-scaling of the web tier is easily achieved by adding or re=
moving servers based on traffic load.</p>
<p>Your website grows rapidly and attracts a significant number of users in=
ternationally. To improve availability and provide a better user experience=
 across wider geographical areas, supporting multiple data centers is cruci=
al.</p>
