<h2 id=3D"millions-of-users-and-beyond">Millions of users and beyond</h2>
<p>Scaling a system is an iterative process. Iterating on what we have lear=
ned in this chapter could get us far. More fine-tuning and new strategies a=
re needed to scale beyond millions of users. For example, you might need to=
 optimize your system and decouple the system to even smaller services. All=
 the techniques learned in this chapter should provide a good foundation to=
 tackle new challenges. To conclude this chapter, we provide a summary of h=
ow we scale our system to support millions of users:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Keep web tier stateless</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Build redundancy at every tier</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Cache data as much as you can</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Support multiple data centers</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Host static assets in CDN</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Scale your data tier by sharding</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Split tiers into individual services</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Monitor your system and use automation tools</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Congratulations on getting this far! Now give yourself a pat on the back=
. Good job!</p>
